# MCP Server Examples

## Notion MCP Server
- Transport: stdio (default for npx)
- Command: npx
- Args: ['-y', '@notionhq/notion-mcp-server']
- Env: NOTION_TOKEN: ${NOTION_API_KEY}
- Hermes config:
  ```yaml
  mcp_servers:
    Notion:
      command: npx
      args:
        - -y
        - '@notionhq/notion-mcp-server'
      env:
        NOTION_TOKEN: ${NOTION_API_KEY}
  ```

## Composio MCP Server
- Transport: http
- URL: https://connect.composio.dev/mcp
- Headers: {} (no auth headers, OAuth handled automatically)
- Hermes config:
  ```yaml
  mcp_servers:
    Composio:
      transport: http
      url: https://connect.composio.dev/mcp
      headers: '{}'
  ```

## Adding a custom stdio MCP server
- Example: A hypothetical `my-mcp-server` package
- Hermes config:
  ```yaml
  mcp_servers:
    MyService:
      command: npx
      args:
        - -y
        - my-mcp-server
      env:
        API_KEY: ${MY_API_KEY}
  ```

## Removing an MCP server
- Hermes config:
  ```bash
  hermes config unset mcp_servers.Notion
  ```